## 180. Final Exam Algorithm

Memorize this sequence:

```text
                 CODING QUESTION
                        |
                        ↓
               READ ALL EXAMPLES
                        |
                        ↓
              INPUT → OUTPUT TABLE
                        |
                        ↓
             CONVERT A-Z → 1-26
                        |
                        ↓
               CALCULATE DIFFERENCE
                        |
              ┌─────────┴─────────┐
              ↓                   ↓
         Constant shift?         NO
              |                   |
             YES                  ↓
              |              Mirror?
              |                   |
              |              Reverse?
              |                   |
              |          Position rearrangement?
              |                   |
              |          Alternating pattern?
              |                   |
              |          Word properties?
              |                   |
              |          Mathematical pattern?
              |                   |
              └──────────┬────────┘
                         ↓
                    VERIFY ALL
                     EXAMPLES
                         |
                         ↓
                   APPLY RULE
                         |
                         ↓
                      ANSWER
```

---

## 181. Final Checklist

Before considering coding-decoding mastered, you should be able to:

- [ ] Convert A–Z to 1–26 instantly.
- [ ] Convert normal alphabet to reverse alphabet.
- [ ] Detect +1, -1, +2, -2 shifts.
- [ ] Handle Z/A wrap-around.
- [ ] Detect alternating shifts.
- [ ] Detect position-dependent shifts.
- [ ] Detect word reversal.
- [ ] Detect position rearrangement.
- [ ] Calculate alphabet sums.
- [ ] Calculate products and differences.
- [ ] Use first/last/middle letters.
- [ ] Use word length.
- [ ] Use vowel/consonant patterns.
- [ ] Solve Chinese coding.
- [ ] Solve substitution coding.
- [ ] Solve operator-symbol coding.
- [ ] Decode matrix coding.
- [ ] Understand binary-style coding.
- [ ] Reverse a multi-step transformation.
- [ ] Verify a rule against every example.
- [ ] Reject rules that only fit one example.
- [ ] Use option elimination efficiently.

---

## 182. Final Concept

The deepest idea behind coding-decoding is:

```text
                OBSERVATION
                     ↓
              REPRESENTATION
                     ↓
              TRANSFORMATION
                     ↓
               RELATIONSHIP
                     ↓
                  PATTERN
                     ↓
                  RULE
                     ↓
              ENCODE / DECODE
```

Do not memorize hundreds of individual codes.

Instead, learn to recognize the **transformation**.

Once you can see:

```text
+1
-1
mirror
reverse
rearrangement
position shift
sum
product
length
frequency
common-word mapping
substitution
conditional rule
```

most coding-decoding questions become mechanical.

---

## 183. One-Line Master Rule

> **Convert the information into a measurable form, compare input with output, find the simplest rule that explains every example, verify it, and only then decode the question.**
